PROCEDURAL NOTE (self-reported near-miss, no defect resulted): my first
master-baseline attempt was `cp -a` + `git checkout master -- web
tailwind.config.js` inside the copy. Worktree `.git` files resolve to the
SAME shared admin dir (.git/worktrees/retiree-refresh) regardless of which
directory copy invokes git, so that checkout touched the shared index. It
was a no-op in effect only because `feat/retiree-refresh` HEAD == `master`
exactly (344cb30, zero commits on the branch) — confirmed via `git
rev-parse master` / `git rev-parse feat/retiree-refresh` both 344cb30 and
`git diff --cached` in the real worktree empty before and after. Switched
to `git archive` (reads objects only, no working-dir/index link) for the
rest of the audit and did not repeat the checkout pattern.

